        "original_id": "ef90e099-ef1b-5ff4-8901-353f9f7574c4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ronnie Van Zant, Mick Jones, Allen Collins\n- Organizations: Lynyrd Skynyrd, The Clash\n- Works: “That Smell”, Street Survivors\n- Roles: lead vocalist, lyricist, guitarist, songwriter, cofounder\n\nFacts:\n- Ronald Wayne Van Zant was born on January 15, 1948.\n- Ronnie Van Zant was an American lead vocalist, primary lyricist, and a founding member of Lynyrd Skynyrd.\n- Mick Jones was born on 26 June 1955.\n- Mick Jones is a British musician, singer, and songwriter who was the lead guitarist, co-lead vocalist, cofounder, and songwriter for The Clash until his dismissal in 1983.\n- “That Smell” was written by Ronnie Van Zant and Allen Collins.\n- “That Smell” was released in 1977 on the album Street Survivors.\n- Ronnie Van Zant died on October 20, 1977.",
